# oracle: superellipsoid granular contact (in.ellipsoid_gran as shipped): a block-2 2 ellipsoid (shape 2 1 1) falling onto a frozen ellipsoid at rest, hooke + linear_history tangential, gravity on the top particle, 3000 steps; per-atom positions, velocities, forces, torques and angular momenta
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): every per-atom column (positions, velocities, forces, torques, angular momenta,
# orientations) and every thermo row agree exactly at the printed precision (max relative error 0).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# oracle-files: oracle_sf.dump
units           si
atom_style      ellipsoid superellipsoid
dimension       3
boundary p p p
comm_modify vel yes
newton off
# create big ellipsoidal particles

region          box block 0 10 0 10 0 10
create_box      2 box
create_atoms 1 single 5 5 4.5
create_atoms 1 single 5 5 6
group bot id 1
group top id 2

set             type 1 mass 1.0
set             type 1 shape 2.0 1.0 1.0
set             type 1 block 2.0 2.0

pair_style      granular/superellipsoid
pair_coeff      * * hooke 1000.0 0.0 tangential linear_history 285 0.0 0.5 damping mass_velocity

compute diameter all property/atom shapex shapey shapez
compute orient all property/atom quatw quati quatj quatk
compute block all property/atom block1 block2

fix 1 bot freeze
fix 2 top gravity 9.81 vector 0 0 -1
fix 3 all nve/asphere

thermo 10
thermo_style custom step pe ke
thermo_modify format float %.15g
timestep 0.001
run             3000
write_dump all custom oracle_sf.dump id type x y z vx vy vz fx fy fz tqx tqy tqz angmomx angmomy angmomz c_orient[*] c_block[*] modify format float %.15g sort id
